-> T26 Phase 2, Decision 3: `∩` on two schemas is inheritance — the set of
-> objects satisfying BOTH. Only possible because schemas are open
-> (structural) — a closed reading would make A ∩ B empty whenever A and B
-> name different fields.
A = { x ∈ Number }
B = { y ∈ String }
C = A ∩ B

obj ∈ C
obj = { x = 1, y = "hi" }
assert obj.x = 1
assert obj.y = "hi"

-> An object satisfying only one half of the intersection doesn't qualify —
-> see fail_object_schema_missing_field.code / the ∩-specific case below.
another ∈ C
another = { x = 5, y = "ok", z = true }
assert another.z = true
